We have a sorted array, and we can expect that sorted array has some duplicates also.
So, given any number, you have to find the first and the last occurrence of that number,
in case it is repeating multiple times in that sorted array.
For example, if you have an array 1, 2, 3, 3, 4, 4, then 5, 5, like this,
if there is a sorted array, and someone gives an input as 3.
So, we have to print the first index position where number 3 is there, and the last index position at which number 3 is occurring.


this is the classic Cookie Assignment Problem (Greedy algorithm), with the twist that:
	•	A child is satisfied only if cookie size == child’s required size (exact match, not ≥).
	•	Each child gets at most one cookie.
	•	Each cookie can be used only once.